# date(1)

## NAME

date - print the date and time

## SYNOPSIS

    date [-u] [+format]

## DESCRIPTION

Prints the current date and time. Time is always UTC (there are no time zones yet). The default format is `%a %b %e %H:%M:%S UTC %Y`.

A format starting with `+` uses strftime conversions: `%Y %C %y %m %d %e %H %I %M %S %p %j %a %A %b %h %B %u %w %s %N %F %T %D %R %Z %z %n %t %%`. Setting the clock is not supported.

## OPTIONS

- `-u`: accepted; the time is always UTC

## EXAMPLES

    date +%F

## SEE ALSO

sleep(1)
